IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `twa-dates`

-- Wills Act 2008 (Tas) -- the rules a person claiming under or against the will of a person who has died meets: what
-- property a will can give (s 6), who could make it and how it had to be signed and witnessed (ss 7, 8, 11, 20, 60),
-- the Court's power to accept an informal document (s 10), gifts to witnesses (ss 12-14), revocation, alteration and
-- revival (ss 15-19), the Tribunal's statutory wills (s 31), rectification and its time limit (s 42), the 30-day
-- survival rule and gifts that fail (ss 45, 49, 55, 56(2)), the right to see the will (s 63) and maintenance in the
-- first 30 days (s 64). What is left out, and why, is in NOTES.md.
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in twa-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("is not valid unless", "only",
-- "may not", "is not revoked", a "where" or "if" condition that fails, "does not apply if"); or NOTHING where the Act
-- does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Judgments the Act leaves to the Court or the
-- Tribunal ("satisfied beyond reasonable doubt", "thinks this is necessary", a contrary intention "established") are
-- inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Wills Act 2008`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is yes` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN JUST b THEN b
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is no` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN JUST b THEN (NOT b)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 6 -- property that may be disposed of by will`

-- s 6(1): "A person may dispose by will of property to which the person is entitled at the time of his or her death."
-- (2): "... property to which the personal representative of that person becomes entitled by virtue of the office of
-- personal representative after the death". (3): it does not matter that the entitlement did not exist when the will
-- was made. (4): "A person may not dispose by will of property of which the person was trustee at the time of the
-- death": a flat negative, JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `Kind of property` IS ONE OF
    `property the will-maker was entitled to at death`
    `property the personal representative became entitled to, as personal representative, after the death`
    `property the will-maker held as trustee at death`

GIVEN `the property` IS A `Kind of property`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 -- the will can dispose of the property` `the property` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the property`
    WHEN `property the will-maker held as trustee at death` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 7 and s 20 -- the will of a minor`

-- s 4: "minor means a person under the age of 18 years". s 7(1): "A will made by a minor is not valid." (2) "Despite
-- subsection (1) -- (a) a minor may make a will in contemplation of marriage ... but the will is of no effect if the
-- marriage contemplated does not take place; and (b) a minor who is married may make, alter or revoke a will". s 20(4):
-- a will made under a Court order authorising a minor "(a) must be executed as required by law and one of the attesting
-- witnesses must be the Registrar; ... (c) is not valid if it is made in breach of any condition". s 20(5): "A will made
-- by a deceased minor according to the law relating to wills of minors of the place where the deceased was resident at
-- the time of execution is a valid will of the deceased."
--
-- JUST TRUE for an adult, and for a minor under one of the heads; JUST FALSE otherwise ("is not valid", "of no effect",
-- "is not valid if"). A Court-authorised will without the Registrar as a witness: a bare "must" not done, JUST FALSE
-- (fork F4). The formal requirements of s 8 are checked separately.
GIVEN `the will-maker's age when the will was made` IS A NUMBER
      `the will-maker was married when the will was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will was made in contemplation of a marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that marriage took place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will was made under a Court order authorising the minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar was one of the attesting witnesses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will was made within the conditions of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 7, 20 -- the will-maker could make the will` `the will-maker's age when the will was made` `the will-maker was married when the will was made` `the will was made in contemplation of a marriage` `that marriage took place` `the will was made under a Court order authorising the minor` `the Registrar was one of the attesting witnesses` `the will was made within the conditions of the order` MEANS
    IF `the will-maker's age when the will was made` AT LEAST 18
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the will was made under a Court order authorising the minor`
         THEN IF `the Registrar was one of the attesting witnesses` AND `the will was made within the conditions of the order`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the will-maker was married when the will was made`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE IF `the will was made in contemplation of a marriage` AND `that marriage took place`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 8 and s 11 -- how a will must be signed and witnessed`

-- s 8(1): "A will is not valid unless -- (a) it is in writing and signed by the testator or by some other person in the
-- presence of and at the direction of the testator; and (b) the signature is made or acknowledged by the testator in
-- the presence of 2 or more witnesses present at the same time; and (c) at least 2 of those witnesses attest and sign
-- the will in the presence of the testator (but not necessarily in the presence of each other)." (2): "The signature
-- ... must be made with the intention of executing the will, but it is not essential that the signature be made at the
-- foot of the will." (3): no attestation clause is needed. s 9: witnesses need not know it was a will. s 11: "A person
-- who is unable to see and attest that a testator has signed a document may not act as a witness": such a person is not
-- counted. "not valid unless": JUST FALSE when a requirement fails.
GIVEN `the will is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was signed by the will-maker, or by another person in the will-maker's presence and at his or her direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature was made with the intention of executing the will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witnesses present together when the will-maker signed or acknowledged the signature` IS A NUMBER
      `the witnesses who could see the signing and signed the will in the will-maker's presence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8 -- the will is executed as the Act requires` `the will is in writing` `it was signed by the will-maker, or by another person in the will-maker's presence and at his or her direction` `the signature was made with the intention of executing the will` `the witnesses present together when the will-maker signed or acknowledged the signature` `the witnesses who could see the signing and signed the will in the will-maker's presence` IF
        `the will is in writing`
    AND `it was signed by the will-maker, or by another person in the will-maker's presence and at his or her direction`
    AND `the signature was made with the intention of executing the will`
    AND `the witnesses present together when the will-maker signed or acknowledged the signature` AT LEAST 2
    AND `the witnesses who could see the signing and signed the will in the will-maker's presence` AT LEAST 2

§§ `ss 7, 8, 20 and 60 -- the will is validly made`

-- s 60(1): "A will is taken to be properly executed if its execution conforms to the internal law in force in the
-- place -- (a) where it was executed; or (b) that was the testator's domicile or habitual residence, either at the time
-- the will was executed, or at the testator's death; or (c) of which the testator was a national ...". s 60 saves the
-- form only; it does not make up for the will-maker's age (s 7). s 20(5) (a deceased minor's will valid under the law of
-- the place of residence) is a statement of validity and is applied first. The Court's power to accept an informal
-- document (s 10) is a separate question.
GIVEN `the will-maker could make the will` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the will-maker was a minor resident elsewhere whose will is valid under that place's law for minors' wills` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will is executed as section 8 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its execution conforms to the internal law of a place section 60 names` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 7, 8, 20, 60 -- the will is validly made` `the will-maker could make the will` `the will-maker was a minor resident elsewhere whose will is valid under that place's law for minors' wills` `the will is executed as section 8 requires` `its execution conforms to the internal law of a place section 60 names` MEANS
    IF `the will-maker was a minor resident elsewhere whose will is valid under that place's law for minors' wills`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `it is no` `the will-maker could make the will`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the will is executed as section 8 requires` OR `its execution conforms to the internal law of a place section 60 names`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 10 -- the Court may dispense with the formalities`

-- s 10(1): "A document or part of a document purporting to embody the testamentary intentions of a deceased person,
-- even though it has not been executed in the manner required by this Act, constitutes a will ..., an alteration ...
-- or the revocation ..., if the Court is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the deceased person intended the
-- document to constitute" it. The Court's satisfaction is an input. "if": JUST FALSE when the Court is not satisfied.
-- A document that does not purport to embody testamentary intentions is outside the section (NOTHING-kind: a scope
-- limit in the text's own wording).
GIVEN `the document purports to embody the deceased's testamentary intentions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the deceased intended it to be his or her will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10 -- the document constitutes the will` `the document purports to embody the deceased's testamentary intentions` `the Court is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the deceased intended it to be his or her will` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document purports to embody the deceased's testamentary intentions`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the Court is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the deceased intended it to be his or her will`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 12 to 14 -- gifts to a witness`

-- s 12(1): "where a beneficial disposition is made by a will to a person who attests the execution of the will, the
-- disposition is void so far only as concerns that person or any person claiming under that person." (2): not void if
-- "(a) more than 2 persons have attested the execution of the will and at least 2 of them are not persons to whom any
-- such disposition is made or the spouses of any such persons; or (b) all the persons who would benefit directly from
-- the avoidance of the disposition consent in writing ... and they all have capacity at law to do so." s 14(2): once a
-- copy of an order declaring that s 12 does not apply is served on the personal representative, "the will ... has
-- effect as if section 12 does not apply". s 13(1): an order "that that person is to be entitled under the will as if
-- that section did not apply".
--
-- The answer is whether the gift is void as to me: JUST TRUE (void), JUST FALSE where the "where" condition fails (I
-- neither attested nor claim under a witness) or a saving applies ("is not made void").
DECLARE `My link to the witnessing` IS ONE OF
    `I attested the will`
    `I claim under a person who attested the will`
    `I neither attested the will nor claim under a person who did`

GIVEN `my link` IS A `My link to the witnessing`
      `the persons who attested the will` IS A NUMBER
      `the attesting persons who were given nothing and are not the spouse of anyone given something` IS A NUMBER
      `everyone who would benefit from the gift failing consented in writing, with capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Court order that section 12 does not apply to the gift has been made and served on the personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 -- the gift is void as to me` `my link` `the persons who attested the will` `the attesting persons who were given nothing and are not the spouse of anyone given something` `everyone who would benefit from the gift failing consented in writing, with capacity` `a Court order that section 12 does not apply to the gift has been made and served on the personal representative` MEANS
    IF `my link` EQUALS `I neither attested the will nor claim under a person who did`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a Court order that section 12 does not apply to the gift has been made and served on the personal representative`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF (`the persons who attested the will` GREATER THAN 2 AND `the attesting persons who were given nothing and are not the spouse of anyone given something` AT LEAST 2)
                 OR `everyone who would benefit from the gift failing consented in writing, with capacity`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 13(2): "An application under this section may be made before the grant of probate of the will but, subject to
-- subsection (3), is not to be made more than 6 months after that date." (3): "The Court may extend the time ...
-- whether or not the time ... has expired, but no application may be made after the final distribution of the estate".
-- "that date" is read as the date of the grant (fork F2). The 6 months end on the corresponding day (fork F1).
--
-- The regulative rule: once probate is granted, the witness must apply WITHIN the days to the end of the 6 months.
-- The rule starts on the day of the grant, so an application on day n is at time n. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is
-- never exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the Court to take the gift as if section 12 did not apply`
    `apply to the Court to rectify the will`

GIVEN `the days to the end of the 6 months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 13(2) -- the witness's 6 months` `the days to the end of the 6 months` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST `apply to the Court to take the gift as if section 12 did not apply`
    WITHIN `the days to the end of the 6 months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "the application under s 13 was not made within 6 months after the grant of probate, and the time has not been extended (s 13(2), (3))"

GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 13(2) -- the last day of the 6 months after the grant` `the day of the grant` MEANS `the corresponding day` 6 `months after` `the day of the grant`

GIVEN `the day I apply` IS A DATE, `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `applying on` `the day I apply` `is within the 6 months after the grant on` `the day of the grant` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 13(2) -- the witness's 6 months` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the Court to take the gift as if section 12 did not apply` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` (`s 13(2) -- the last day of the 6 months after the grant` `the day of the grant`)
        `the time of the step` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` `the day I apply`

-- Whether an application made on a day is allowed. "no application may be made after the final distribution": JUST
-- FALSE. Before the grant: JUST TRUE ("may be made before the grant"). Within the 6 months: JUST TRUE. After them:
-- JUST TRUE if the Court extends the time (its judgment, an input), JUST FALSE if not ("is not to be made").
GIVEN `probate has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE
      `the estate had been finally distributed before I applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court extends the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 13(2), (3) -- I may apply on that day` `probate has been granted` `the day of the grant` `the day I apply` `the estate had been finally distributed before I applied` `the Court extends the time` MEANS
    IF `the estate had been finally distributed before I applied`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT `probate has been granted`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` `the day I apply` LESS THAN 0
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE IF `applying on` `the day I apply` `is within the 6 months after the grant on` `the day of the grant`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE IF `the Court extends the time`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 14(1): "Where the Court is satisfied that the entitlement of the applicant under the will was known to and
-- approved by the testator and was not included in the will as the result of fraud, duress or the exercise of undue
-- influence by any person, the Court may, by order, declare that section 12 does not apply". (3): the applicant may not
-- rely on any evidentiary presumption that the testator knew and approved. A "where" condition: JUST FALSE when it
-- fails. "may" leaves the order to the Court: JUST TRUE means the Court may make it.
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied the will-maker knew of and approved my gift` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied my gift was not the result of fraud, duress or undue influence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1) -- the Court may declare that section 12 does not apply to me` `the Court is satisfied the will-maker knew of and approved my gift` `the Court is satisfied my gift was not the result of fraud, duress or undue influence` MEANS
    IF `the Court is satisfied the will-maker knew of and approved my gift` AND `the Court is satisfied my gift was not the result of fraud, duress or undue influence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 15 -- how a will may be revoked`

-- s 15(1): "The whole or any part of a will may be revoked only -- (a) in the circumstances mentioned in Division 1 or
-- 2 of Part 3 or by the operation of section 16 or 17; or (b) by a later will; or (c) by some writing declaring an
-- intention to revoke it, executed in the manner in which a will is required to be executed ...; or (d) by the
-- testator, or some person in his or her presence and by his or her direction, burning, tearing or otherwise destroying
-- it with the intention of the testator of revoking it; or (e) by the testator, or some person in his or her presence
-- and by his or her direction, writing on the will or dealing with the will in such a manner that the Court is satisfied
-- from the state of the will that the testator intended to revoke it." (2): "A will is not revoked by a presumption of
-- intention on the ground of an alteration in circumstances." A list closed with "only", and a flat negative: JUST
-- FALSE for anything else. s 10 lets the Court accept an informal document as a revocation.
DECLARE `What was done to the will` IS ONE OF
    `a later will revoked it`
    `a writing declaring an intention to revoke it was executed as a will must be`
    `a document the Court accepts under section 10 revoked it`
    `the will-maker burnt, tore or otherwise destroyed it`
    `another person burnt, tore or destroyed it in the will-maker's presence and at his or her direction`
    `another person burnt, tore or destroyed it, not in the will-maker's presence or not at his or her direction`
    `the will-maker, or another person in his or her presence and at his or her direction, wrote on it or dealt with it`
    `a Court order for a minor or for a person lacking capacity revoked it`
    `the will-maker's circumstances changed`
    `nothing was done to it`

GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What was done to the will`
      `the will-maker intended to revoke it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied from the state of the will that the will-maker intended to revoke it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 -- the will has been revoked` `what was done` `the will-maker intended to revoke it` `the Court is satisfied from the state of the will that the will-maker intended to revoke it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what was done`
    WHEN `a later will revoked it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a writing declaring an intention to revoke it was executed as a will must be` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a document the Court accepts under section 10 revoked it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Court order for a minor or for a person lacking capacity revoked it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the will-maker burnt, tore or otherwise destroyed it` THEN
        IF `the will-maker intended to revoke it` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `another person burnt, tore or destroyed it in the will-maker's presence and at his or her direction` THEN
        IF `the will-maker intended to revoke it` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the will-maker, or another person in his or her presence and at his or her direction, wrote on it or dealt with it` THEN
        IF `the Court is satisfied from the state of the will that the will-maker intended to revoke it` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 16 -- marriage or a registered relationship revokes a will`

-- s 16(1): "A will is revoked by -- (a) the marriage of the testator; or (b) the registration of a deed of relationship
-- under Part 2 of the Relationships Act 2003 to which the testator is a party." (2): not revoked: "(a) a disposition to
-- the person to whom the testator is married or with whom the testator is in a registered relationship at the time of
-- his or her death; (b) any appointment as executor, trustee, advisory trustee or guardian of" that person; "(c) a will
-- made in exercise of a power of appointment, if the property so appointed would not pass to the executor ... or the
-- administrator ... if the power ... was not exercised." (3): a will made in contemplation of the marriage or
-- registration, expressed or not, "is not revoked by" it. (4): "A will that is expressed to be made in contemplation of
-- marriage generally or the registration of a deed of relationship ... is not revoked by the solemnisation of a marriage
-- of the testator or the registration of a deed of relationship" (fork F5: either general expression read as saving
-- the will from either event). s 4: "disposition" includes the creation by will of a power of appointment.
--
-- The answer is whether the will is revoked as to my benefit: JUST TRUE (revoked), JUST FALSE where a saving applies
-- ("are not revoked", "is not revoked") or where there was no marriage or registration after the will.
GIVEN `the will-maker married, or registered a deed of relationship, after making the will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was the will-maker's spouse or registered partner by that marriage or deed at his or her death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will exercises a power of appointment over property that would not otherwise pass to the executor or administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will was made in contemplation of that marriage or registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage, or of registering a deed of relationship, generally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16 -- the will is revoked as to my benefit by the marriage or registration` `the will-maker married, or registered a deed of relationship, after making the will` `I was the will-maker's spouse or registered partner by that marriage or deed at his or her death` `the will exercises a power of appointment over property that would not otherwise pass to the executor or administrator` `the will was made in contemplation of that marriage or registration` `the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage, or of registering a deed of relationship, generally` MEANS
    IF NOT `the will-maker married, or registered a deed of relationship, after making the will`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the will was made in contemplation of that marriage or registration`
              OR `the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage, or of registering a deed of relationship, generally`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `I was the will-maker's spouse or registered partner by that marriage or deed at his or her death`
                   OR `the will exercises a power of appointment over property that would not otherwise pass to the executor or administrator`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 17 -- the end of a marriage or a registered relationship`

-- s 17(1): the ending of the testator's marriage, or the revocation of a registered deed of relationship, "revokes --
-- (a) any beneficial disposition made by a testator to the testator's spouse in a will in existence at the time the
-- marriage ends or the deed of relationship is revoked; and (b) any appointment of the testator's spouse as an
-- executor, trustee, advisory trustee or guardian made by the will; and (c) any grant made by the will of a power of
-- appointment exercisable by, or in favour of, the testator's spouse." (2): it does not revoke "(a) the appointment of
-- the testator's spouse as trustee of property left by the will on trust for beneficiaries that include the spouse's
-- children; or (b) the grant of a power of appointment exercisable by the testator's spouse exclusively in favour of the
-- children of whom both the testator and spouse are parents." (3): the will takes effect as if the spouse had died
-- before the testator. (4): "Subsection (1) does not apply if a contrary intention appears in the will or can otherwise
-- be established." (5): "a marriage ends -- (a) when a decree of dissolution ... becomes absolute under the Family Law
-- Act 1975 ...; or (b) on the granting of a decree of nullity ... by the Family Court of Australia; or (c) on the
-- dissolution or annulment ... in accordance with the law of a place outside Australia, but only if that dissolution
-- or annulment is recognised in Australia".
--
-- JUST TRUE (revoked); JUST FALSE where (2) saves the benefit, where (4)'s contrary intention is found (an input), for a
-- foreign dissolution not recognised ("but only if"), for a will made after the ending ("in existence at the time"),
-- for a separation without a divorce (s 17(5) read as saying when a marriage ends, fork F6), and where nothing has
-- ended. The ending of an unregistered significant relationship: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: the text is silent; s 17 names
-- only marriage and a registered deed, though s 4's "spouse" includes a significant relationship; finding 3).
DECLARE `How the relationship ended` IS ONE OF
    `a divorce became absolute under the Family Law Act 1975`
    `the Family Court granted a decree of nullity`
    `it was dissolved or annulled outside Australia and that is recognised in Australia`
    `it was dissolved or annulled outside Australia and that is not recognised in Australia`
    `our registered deed of relationship was revoked under the Relationships Act 2003`
    `we separated but the marriage was not dissolved`
    `an unregistered significant relationship ended`
    `it has not ended`

DECLARE `My benefit under the will` IS ONE OF
    `a gift of property`
    `an appointment as executor, trustee, advisory trustee or guardian`
    `an appointment as trustee of property left on trust for beneficiaries who include my children`
    `a power of appointment exercisable by me or in my favour`
    `a power of appointment exercisable by me only in favour of children of whom the will-maker and I are both parents`

GIVEN `how it ended` IS A `How the relationship ended`
      `the will was in existence when the relationship ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my benefit` IS A `My benefit under the will`
      `a contrary intention appears in the will or is established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 -- the ending revokes my benefit` `how it ended` `the will was in existence when the relationship ended` `my benefit` `a contrary intention appears in the will or is established` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how it ended`
    WHEN `an unregistered significant relationship ended` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `it was dissolved or annulled outside Australia and that is not recognised in Australia` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `we separated but the marriage was not dissolved` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `it has not ended` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF NOT `the will was in existence when the relationship ended`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears in the will or is established`
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE CONSIDER `my benefit`
                  WHEN `an appointment as trustee of property left on trust for beneficiaries who include my children` THEN JUST FALSE
                  WHEN `a power of appointment exercisable by me only in favour of children of whom the will-maker and I are both parents` THEN JUST FALSE
                  OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 18 -- alterations`

-- s 18(1): "An obliteration, interlineation or other alteration made in any will after the execution of the will is
-- not valid, except so far as the words or effect of the will before the alteration are not apparent, unless the
-- alteration is executed in accordance with Division 2 of this Part or Division 2 of Part 3." (2): an alteration is
-- duly executed if the signature and the witnesses' subscription are "in the margin or on some other part of the will
-- opposite or near to the alteration" or at a memorandum referring to it. s 10 lets the Court accept an informal
-- alteration. Three answers: the alteration counts; only the obliteration counts (the original words are not
-- apparent, so they are gone, but nothing written in their place counts); or the will reads as it did.
DECLARE `Effect of the alteration` IS ONE OF
    `the alteration counts as part of the will`
    `the original words are gone, but nothing written in their place counts`
    `the alteration does not count and the will reads as before`

GIVEN `the alteration was signed and witnessed as a will must be, near it or at a memorandum referring to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration was made under a Court order for a person lacking testamentary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court accepts the alteration under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the words before the alteration are still apparent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Effect of the alteration`
`s 18 -- the effect of the alteration` `the alteration was signed and witnessed as a will must be, near it or at a memorandum referring to it` `the alteration was made under a Court order for a person lacking testamentary capacity` `the Court accepts the alteration under section 10` `the words before the alteration are still apparent` MEANS
    IF `the alteration was signed and witnessed as a will must be, near it or at a memorandum referring to it`
       OR `the alteration was made under a Court order for a person lacking testamentary capacity`
       OR `the Court accepts the alteration under section 10`
    THEN `the alteration counts as part of the will`
    ELSE IF `the words before the alteration are still apparent`
         THEN `the alteration does not count and the will reads as before`
         ELSE `the original words are gone, but nothing written in their place counts`

§§ `s 19 -- revival`

-- s 19(1): "A will or part of a will that has been revoked is revived by re-execution or by execution of a will showing
-- an intention to revive the will or part." (4): a revived will "is taken to have been executed on the date on which
-- the will is revived". The text names two ways and does not close the list with "only": JUST TRUE for either, NOTHING
-- otherwise (NOTHING-kind: the text lists without closing the list).
GIVEN `the will-maker re-executed the revoked will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will-maker executed a later will showing an intention to revive it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19 -- the revoked will is revived` `the will-maker re-executed the revoked will` `the will-maker executed a later will showing an intention to revive it` MEANS
    IF `the will-maker re-executed the revoked will` OR `the will-maker executed a later will showing an intention to revive it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 31 -- the Tribunal's statutory will and an earlier will`

-- s 31: "A statutory will made by the Tribunal is invalid if there exists a prior will, which is not a statutory will
-- made by the Tribunal or the Guardianship and Administration Board ..., of the person for whom it is made." s 39: a
-- statutory will "has the same effect for all purposes as if" the person were capable and had executed it under
-- Division 2 of Part 2. JUST FALSE ("invalid if") where such a prior will exists; otherwise JUST TRUE, on the footing
-- that the Tribunal's order was made (its s 33 findings are not for the person in this seat to state).
GIVEN `the person had made an earlier will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that earlier will was itself a statutory will made by the Tribunal or the former Guardianship and Administration Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31 -- the Tribunal's statutory will is valid` `the person had made an earlier will` `that earlier will was itself a statutory will made by the Tribunal or the former Guardianship and Administration Board` MEANS
    IF `the person had made an earlier will` AND (NOT `that earlier will was itself a statutory will made by the Tribunal or the former Guardianship and Administration Board`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 42 -- rectification`

-- s 42(1): "The Court may make an order to rectify a will to carry out the intentions of the testator if the Court is
-- satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the will does not carry out the testator's intentions because -- (a) a
-- clerical error was made; or (b) the will does not give effect to the testator's instructions." (2): "A person who
-- wishes to make an application for an order under this section must apply to the Court within 3 months after the date
-- of the death of the testator." (3): "The Court may extend the period ... if the Court thinks this is necessary, even
-- if the original period of time has expired, but not if the final distribution of the estate has been made."
DECLARE `Why the will misses the will-maker's intentions` IS ONE OF
    `a clerical error was made`
    `the will does not give effect to the will-maker's instructions`
    `another reason`

-- An "if ... because" condition: JUST FALSE when it fails.
GIVEN `why` IS A `Why the will misses the will-maker's intentions`
      `the Court is satisfied of it beyond reasonable doubt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(1) -- the Court may rectify the will` `why` `the Court is satisfied of it beyond reasonable doubt` MEANS
    IF `why` EQUALS `another reason`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the Court is satisfied of it beyond reasonable doubt`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The regulative rule: the applicant MUST apply WITHIN the days to the end of the 3 months after the death (the
-- corresponding day, fork F1). The rule starts on the day of the death, so an application on day n is at time n.
GIVEN `the days to the end of the 3 months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 42(2) -- the 3 months to apply for rectification` `the days to the end of the 3 months` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST `apply to the Court to rectify the will`
    WITHIN `the days to the end of the 3 months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "the application for rectification was not made within 3 months after the date of the death (s 42(2))"

GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 42(2) -- the last day of the 3 months after the death` `the day of the death` MEANS `the corresponding day` 3 `months after` `the day of the death`

GIVEN `the day I apply` IS A DATE, `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `applying on` `the day I apply` `is within the 3 months after the death on` `the day of the death` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 42(2) -- the 3 months to apply for rectification` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the Court to rectify the will` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the death` `to` (`s 42(2) -- the last day of the 3 months after the death` `the day of the death`)
        `the time of the step` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the death` `to` `the day I apply`

-- Within the 3 months: JUST TRUE. After them: JUST FALSE if the estate has been finally distributed ("but not if");
-- otherwise JUST TRUE if the Court extends the time (its judgment, an input), JUST FALSE if not. An application on a
-- day before the death is not a case the section meets: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: the text is silent).
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE
      `the estate had been finally distributed before I applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court extends the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 42(2), (3) -- my application to rectify is in time` `the day of the death` `the day I apply` `the estate had been finally distributed before I applied` `the Court extends the time` MEANS
    IF `the days from` `the day of the death` `to` `the day I apply` LESS THAN 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `applying on` `the day I apply` `is within the 3 months after the death on` `the day of the death`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the estate had been finally distributed before I applied`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF `the Court extends the time`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 42(4): "A personal representative who makes a distribution to a beneficiary is not liable if -- (a) the
-- distribution is made under section 64; or (b) the distribution is made -- (i) at a time when the personal
-- representative was not aware of any application for rectification or any application having been made under the
-- Testator's Family Maintenance Act 1912; and (ii) at least 3 months after the death of the testator." JUST TRUE (not
-- liable) where (a) or (b) holds. Otherwise the Act does not say the personal representative is liable: NOTHING
-- (NOTHING-kind: the text is silent). "at least 3 months after": on or after the corresponding day (fork F1), so a
-- distribution on that day is protected though an application that day is still in time (finding 6).
GIVEN `the distribution was a maintenance distribution under section 64` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal representative knew of a rectification or family maintenance application when distributing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE
      `the day of the distribution` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(4) -- the personal representative is not liable for the distribution` `the distribution was a maintenance distribution under section 64` `the personal representative knew of a rectification or family maintenance application when distributing` `the day of the death` `the day of the distribution` MEANS
    IF `the distribution was a maintenance distribution under section 64`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT `the personal representative knew of a rectification or family maintenance application when distributing`)
            AND `the days from` (`s 42(2) -- the last day of the 3 months after the death` `the day of the death`) `to` `the day of the distribution` AT LEAST 0
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 45 -- a gift that fails falls into the residue`

-- s 45(1): "To the extent that any disposition of property in a will, other than the exercise of a power of
-- appointment, is ineffective wholly or in part, the will takes effect as if the property or the undisposed part of the
-- property were part of the residuary estate of the testator." (2): "This section does not apply if a contrary
-- intention appears in the will." JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE for a contrary intention ("does not apply if"); NOTHING for the
-- exercise of a power of appointment ("other than X", decided case by case: the section does not speak, fork F7).
GIVEN `the failed gift was the exercise of a power of appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears in the will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45 -- the failed gift falls into the residue` `the failed gift was the exercise of a power of appointment` `a contrary intention appears in the will` MEANS
    IF `the failed gift was the exercise of a power of appointment`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears in the will`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 49 -- a beneficiary must survive the will-maker by 30 days`

-- s 49(1): "If a disposition is made in a will to a person who dies within 30 days after the death of the testator, the
-- will is to take effect as if the person had died immediately before the testator." (2): not if a contrary intention
-- appears in the will. (3): "A general requirement or condition that a beneficiary survive the testator does not
-- indicate a contrary intention". "within 30 days after": days 1 to 30 after the will-maker's death (the day of the
-- death excluded, fork F3). JUST TRUE (the gift fails as to that person) on days 1 to 30; JUST FALSE from day 31 (a
-- period the text fixes) or for a contrary intention. A beneficiary who died before the will-maker, or on the same day,
-- is outside s 49: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: a scope limit in the text's own wording; the gift lapses at common law and
-- s 55 may save it for the beneficiary's issue).
GIVEN `the day the will-maker died` IS A DATE
      `the day the beneficiary died` IS A DATE
      `a contrary intention appears in the will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 -- the will takes effect as if the beneficiary died first` `the day the will-maker died` `the day the beneficiary died` `a contrary intention appears in the will` MEANS
    IF `the days after` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears in the will`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the days after` AT MOST 30
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the days after` MEANS `the days from` `the day the will-maker died` `to` `the day the beneficiary died`

§§ `s 55 -- the issue of a child who dies first take the child's share`

-- s 55(1): the section applies if "(a) a testator makes a disposition of property to a person ... who is issue of the
-- testator (... an original beneficiary); and (b) under the will, the interest of the original beneficiary ... does not
-- come to an end at or before the original beneficiary's death; and (c) the disposition is not a disposition of
-- property to the testator's issue, without limitation as to remoteness; and (d) the original beneficiary does not
-- survive the testator for 30 days." (2): "The issue of the original beneficiary who survive the testator for 30 days
-- take the original beneficiary's share ... as if the original beneficiary had died intestate leaving only issue
-- surviving." (3): not if "(a) the original beneficiary did not fulfil a condition imposed ... in the will; or (b) a
-- contrary intention appears in the will". (4), (5): a general condition that issue survive or reach an age, and a gift
-- to issue as joint tenants, do not of themselves show a contrary intention.
--
-- "survive the testator for 30 days": alive at the end of the 30th day after the death (fork F3). Whether I would share
-- in the original beneficiary's estate on an intestacy leaving only issue is the intestacy law's (the Intestacy
-- Act 2010, not deposited), asked as a fact; how big my part is follows from it and is not computed here. JUST TRUE (I take
-- in place of the original beneficiary); JUST FALSE where an "if" fails or (3) applies.
GIVEN `the original beneficiary is the will-maker's child or other issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the original beneficiary's interest would not end at or before his or her death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gift is to the will-maker's issue without limitation as to remoteness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the will-maker died` IS A DATE
      `the day the original beneficiary died` IS A DATE
      `I would share in the original beneficiary's estate on an intestacy leaving only issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I survived the will-maker for 30 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the original beneficiary did not fulfil a condition the will imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears in the will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55 -- I take the original beneficiary's share` `the original beneficiary is the will-maker's child or other issue` `the original beneficiary's interest would not end at or before his or her death` `the gift is to the will-maker's issue without limitation as to remoteness` `the day the will-maker died` `the day the original beneficiary died` `I would share in the original beneficiary's estate on an intestacy leaving only issue` `I survived the will-maker for 30 days` `the original beneficiary did not fulfil a condition the will imposed` `a contrary intention appears in the will` MEANS
    IF NOT `the section applies`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the original beneficiary did not fulfil a condition the will imposed` OR `a contrary intention appears in the will`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `I would share in the original beneficiary's estate on an intestacy leaving only issue` AND `I survived the will-maker for 30 days`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the section applies` MEANS
                `the original beneficiary is the will-maker's child or other issue`
            AND `the original beneficiary's interest would not end at or before his or her death`
            AND (NOT `the gift is to the will-maker's issue without limitation as to remoteness`)
            AND `the days from` `the day the will-maker died` `to` `the day the original beneficiary died` AT MOST 30

§§ `s 56(2) -- a failed fraction of the residue`

-- s 56(2): "If any part of a disposition in fractional parts of the whole or of the residue of the estate of a testator
-- fails, the part that fails passes to the part that does not fail, and, if there is more than one part that does not
-- fail, to all those parts proportionately." (3): not if a contrary intention appears in the will. My new fraction is my
-- fraction plus my proportionate part of the failed fractions: mine x all / (all - failed). A contrary intention: NOTHING
-- (the will governs; NOTHING-kind: the section does not apply and the Act does not say what happens instead). Every part
-- failing, or the failed parts given as more than the whole: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: the text is silent).
GIVEN `my fraction` IS A NUMBER
      `all the fractions in the gift` IS A NUMBER
      `the fractions that failed` IS A NUMBER
      `a contrary intention appears in the will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 56(2) -- my fraction after the failed parts pass` `my fraction` `all the fractions in the gift` `the fractions that failed` `a contrary intention appears in the will` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears in the will`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the fractions that remain` AT MOST 0
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST ((`my fraction` TIMES `all the fractions in the gift`) DIVIDED BY `the fractions that remain`)
    WHERE
        `the fractions that remain` MEANS `all the fractions in the gift` MINUS `the fractions that failed`

§§ `s 63 -- who may see the will`

-- s 63(1): a person with possession or control of a will (including a revoked or purported will) or a copy "of a
-- deceased person must allow any or all of the following persons to inspect and, at their own expense, take copies of
-- it: (a) any person named or referred to in it, whether as beneficiary or not; (b) the surviving spouse, any parent or
-- guardian and any issue of the testator; (c) any person who would be entitled to a share of the estate ... if the
-- testator had died intestate; (d) any creditor or other person having any claim at law or in equity against the
-- estate ...; (e) any beneficiaries of prior wills ...; (f) a parent or guardian of a minor referred to in the will or
-- who would be entitled to a share ... on an intestacy." (3): "Nothing in this section authorises the inspection ...
-- while the testator is alive." (4): "Nothing in this section limits the rights of a person under any other law."
-- JUST TRUE for a listed person after the death; JUST FALSE while the will-maker is alive (a flat negative); NOTHING
-- for anyone else (NOTHING-kind: the list is not closed with "only", and s 63(4) keeps other law).
DECLARE `My connection to the will` IS ONE OF
    `I am named or referred to in it`
    `I am the will-maker's surviving spouse`
    `I am a parent or guardian of the will-maker`
    `I am the will-maker's child or other issue`
    `I would share in the estate on an intestacy`
    `I am a creditor or have another claim against the estate`
    `I am a beneficiary under an earlier will`
    `I am a parent or guardian of a minor named in the will or who would share on an intestacy`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the will-maker has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my connection` IS A `My connection to the will`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63 -- I may inspect and copy the will` `the will-maker has died` `my connection` MEANS
    IF NOT `the will-maker has died`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `my connection` EQUALS `none of these`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 64 -- maintenance in the first 30 days`

-- s 64(1): "If a surviving person who is wholly or substantially dependent on the testator has an entitlement under a
-- will that does not become absolute until 30 days after the testator's death, the personal representative may make a
-- distribution for the maintenance, support or education of that person within that 30-day period." (2): the personal
-- representative is not liable for one made in good faith; (3): even knowing of a pending family maintenance
-- application. "within that 30-day period": from the day of the death to the 30th day after it (fork F3). JUST TRUE
-- (the personal representative may pay); JUST FALSE where an "if" condition fails or the day is outside the period.
GIVEN `I was wholly or substantially dependent on the will-maker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my entitlement under the will becomes absolute only 30 days after the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is for my maintenance, support or education` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the will-maker died` IS A DATE
      `the day of the payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(1) -- the personal representative may pay me maintenance on that day` `I was wholly or substantially dependent on the will-maker` `my entitlement under the will becomes absolute only 30 days after the death` `the payment is for my maintenance, support or education` `the day the will-maker died` `the day of the payment` MEANS
    IF `I was wholly or substantially dependent on the will-maker`
       AND `my entitlement under the will becomes absolute only 30 days after the death`
       AND `the payment is for my maintenance, support or education`
       AND `the days after` AT LEAST 0
       AND `the days after` AT MOST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the days after` MEANS `the days from` `the day the will-maker died` `to` `the day of the payment`

-- s 64(4): "Any sum distributed is to be deducted from any share of the estate to which the person receiving the
-- distribution becomes entitled, but, if any person to whom any distribution has been made does not survive the
-- testator for 30 days, any such distribution is to be treated as an administration expense." The amount taken off my
-- share: all of it if I survive the 30 days, nothing (an administration expense) if I do not.
GIVEN `the maintenance paid to me` IS A NUMBER
      `I survived the will-maker for 30 days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 64(4) -- the amount taken off my share` `the maintenance paid to me` `I survived the will-maker for 30 days` MEANS
    IF `I survived the will-maker for 30 days`
    THEN `the maintenance paid to me`
    ELSE 0
